config NET_ETH_XDMA_NET
	tristate "AMD/Xilinx XDMA net device"
	depends on m
	help
	  Uses an instance of Xilinx's XDMA block to implement a
	  standard Linux net device. Southbound channels must be
	  attached to AXI stream interfaces, over which Ethernet
	  frames are transported.

	  In contrast to the upstream driver for this core
	  (`drivers/dma/xilinx/xdma.c`), the "Credit Mode" is used to
	  operate the engine with a ring of descriptors, which is much
	  more natural to the kernel's networking API since most NICs
	  operate in this manner.
